{
  "revision": "R161O",
  "scope": "Unfinished joint working board with local circuit restoration.\n\nKeep both clamps and the complete existing wheel-power branch unchanged. Move\nC1501 beside U1501 and put R1504 in its former place. All source ground vias,\nmechanical interfaces, native rules and zone allocations are retained.\nLong detector outputs, OV upstream, the UV divider and UV filter still need\ncomplete routes and manufacturer-layout review. Never adopt this partial board.\n\nRefine C from measured native keepout polygons and DRC, not inferred radii.\nThe detector's six unfinished upstream/output/filter links remain incomplete.\n\nRefine D using actual native keepouts and localized reference-gap geometry.\nAll six unfinished links remain open and no acceptance is implied.\n\nJoint C1301/R1503 F-face placement and actual short UV filter connection.\nReturns to the electrically preserved E working layout. The four mutually\nincompatible raster proposals in F are not reused. No adoption is implied.\n\nResolve G courtyard/land clearance and separate OV from the mid-node antipad.\nKeep the source fixed ground holes and mount keepout; move only the declared\nnon-ground transfer and restore all its native layer branches explicitly.\n\nUse one 45-degree VDD escape and preserve native land/via clearances.\nH already retained all power/reference checks; two measured local conflicts\nare corrected here without relaxing any native rule or altering ground vias.\n\nRetire two complete dead transfer branches left by the explicit relocation.\nAll source terminal-to-terminal copper is retained. These tails now end at\nunused transfer holes, after the old U1301/R1311 escapes were explicitly\nremoved in E. Replacement circuit links remain unfinished, preventing adoption.\n\nTest only the power-aware OV proposal on J; other independent paths omitted.\nSnap transfers to native centres and retain the original design-rule set.\nNative refill must decide whether the diagnosed power cuts are acceptable.\n\nJointly shorten the old ACT_UV escape and move one non-ground transfer 0.1 mm.\nThis opens a grounded F-face OV corridor around both existing transfer holes,\ninstead of cutting the J401 ground thermal or its In2 wheel-power feed.\nAll original ground transfers and circuit pin nets are retained.\n\nLeave the lower J401 ground-spoke outlet open and clear the measured PTH reference void.\nThe F-side OV rail stays farther left through the ground-pad channel; its In2\ndiagonal moves 0.05 mm around the existing plated-hole reference boundary.\n\nClear the native slot-reference boundary and retire two obsolete transfers.\nThe old FAULT dead branch stops at the retained multi-layer 45.7 mm junction;\nthe old OV hole is redundant with the new upstream transfer and continuous B\ntracks. All replacement links still require completion before adoption.\n",
  "board_sha256": "bf719a717ffba2a1468126f6a71a1cc3703980fedf647caf8af07c1a9cef62a0",
